            'The infraspinatus and teres minor are external rotators and the subscapularis an internal rotator. The tendons of these muscles form a supporting arrangement fused with the capsule. The teres major, although it takes part in adduction, internal rotation and extension, is not part of the cuff. In the subacromial region the tendons and the bursa are neighbours between the acromion–coracoacromial arch and the humerus. During movement the conditions of this space depend on the scapula and the humerus being oriented together.',
