            'The long head of the triceps arises from the scapula and its other heads from the humerus; the common attachment is the olecranon. Thus all the heads extend the elbow while only the long head also crosses the shoulder joint. The coracobrachialis extends from the coracoid to the humerus and does not reach the elbow; having “brachii” in its name or an arm relationship does not mean every arm muscle will move the elbow. Following the joints a muscle crosses is one of the most reliable ways of learning its function.',
