            'The gluteus maximus takes part in powerful hip extension, especially when straightening from flexion; it has connections with the iliotibial tract and the femur. The tensor fasciae latae contributes to hip–knee control through the iliotibial tract. The iliopsoas reaches the lesser trochanter through the common distal path of the psoas major and iliacus; it is an important hip flexor. The piriformis, obturator internus/externus, gemelli and quadratus femoris are assessed within the short external rotator group; some of their effects change with the joint angle.',
