            'In the medial thigh the different parts of the adductor magnus may contribute differently to flexion or extension because of their fibre directions. The name “adductor” states the main function but does not exclude all additional effects. The pes anserinus tendons bring together the sartorius, gracilis and semitendinosus coming from three different muscle groups. A common distal attachment does not mean that all the proximal effects of these muscles are the same; one is related to abduction at the hip and another to adduction.',
