            'The gastrocnemius crosses the knee and the ankle, and the soleus only the ankle. This difference explains why knee position changes the length of the gastrocnemius. The deep posterior tendons pass behind the medial malleolus; the tibialis posterior takes part in supporting the arch and the long flexors in the push-off of the toes. The Achilles tendon is the basic common force path of the gastrocnemius and soleus; it is not the tendon of all the posterior muscles of the leg.',
